---
// The explainer around the browser preview. The preview itself is rustyAC's own site, unpacked into
// public/play/app/ by scripts/fetch-web-preview.mjs before the build; this page links to it.
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ImageFigure from '../components/ImageFigure.astro';
import webSpa from '../assets/screenshots/web_spa.webp';
import { LINKS } from '../lib/site';
import { getLatestRelease } from '../lib/release';

const latest = await getLatestRelease();

// VERSION is written by the fetch script next to the unpacked site. No file: the download never worked.
const version = existsSync('public/play/app/index.html')
  ? (await readFile('public/play/app/VERSION', 'utf8').catch(() => '')).trim()
  : '';
const available = version !== '';

const description =
  "Try rustyAC in your browser: the same physics compiled to WebAssembly, bit-exact with the desktop build. You open your own Assetto Corsa folder; nothing is uploaded.";

const TOC = [
  { id: 'what', label: 'What it is' },
  { id: 'need', label: 'What you need' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Your files stay with you' },
  { id: 'controls', label: 'Controls' },
];

// rustyAC docs/web.md, "Keys and pad"
const CONTROLS: [string, string, string][] = [
  ['Throttle, brake', 'Up / W, Down / S', 'RT, LT'],
  ['Steer', 'Left / A, Right / D', 'left stick'],
  ['Gear up, down', 'Space / E, Left Ctrl / Q', 'Y, X'],
  ['Clutch, handbrake', 'Left Shift, B', 'A, RB'],
  ['DRS, KERS / ERS', 'F, K', 'LB, B'],
  ['Traction control up, down', 'T, Shift+T', 'D-pad up, down'],
  ['ABS up, down', 'Y, Shift+Y', 'Back held + D-pad up, down'],
  ['Brake bias forward, rearward', '], [', 'D-pad right, left'],
  ['Back to the pits', 'R', 'Back, a tap'],
  ['Back onto the track', 'Shift+R', 'Back, held 0.6 s and let go'],
  ['Next view', 'F1 or C', 'right stick press'],
  ['New car, automatic gearbox', 'N, G', ''],
  ['Pause, menu, the key list', 'P, Esc, H', 'Start'],
];
---

<Page
  title="Play in your browser"
  intro="The same physics as the desktop build, compiled to WebAssembly and running in a browser tab. It is a preview."
  description={description}
  toc={TOC}
>
  <section class="launch card">
    {
      available ? (
        <>
          <div class="launch__desktop">
            <a class="btn btn--primary launch__btn" href="/play/app/">
              Launch the preview
              <Icon name="arrow" />
            </a>
            <p class="mono muted launch__meta">rustyAC {version} · Chrome or Edge · your own Assetto Corsa folder</p>
          </div>
          <div class="launch__phone">
            <p class="launch__title">Open this on a computer.</p>
            <p class="muted">
              The preview needs a keyboard or a gamepad, and the Assetto Corsa folder on your computer. It does not
              run on a phone.
            </p>
          </div>
        </>
      ) : (
        <div>
          <p class="launch__title">The preview is unavailable right now.</p>
          <p class="muted">
            You can still get it from the <a href={latest.url} rel="noopener">latest release</a>: download the
            <code>-web.zip</code>, unpack it and serve the folder from your own computer.
          </p>
        </div>
      )
    }
  </section>

  <ImageFigure
    src={webSpa}
    alt="The browser preview: a Ferrari F2004 seen from behind on the track at Spa, with the lap time, gear, speed and revs on the display"
    caption="The preview in Chrome: the F2004 at Spa, 60 frames and 333 physics steps a second."
    sizes="(min-width: 1184px) 856px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 328px), (min-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 48px), calc(100vw - 32px)"
  />

  <h2 id="what">What it is</h2>
  <!-- rustyAC docs/web.md intro; docs/port/web.md section 3.2 (160 drives, 1,787,777 steps) and the self-test (10,000 steps, three car and track pairs) -->
  <p>
    The preview is rustyAC's physics, the same Rust code as the desktop build, compiled to WebAssembly. It is
    bit-exact with the desktop: 160 recorded drives (1,787,777 physics steps) were replayed through the WebAssembly
    build and every step matched. In the browser itself, a 10,000-step test drive on three car and track pairs ends
    in the same state as on the desktop.
  </p>
  <h3>What it is not</h3>
  <!-- docs/web.md intro; docs/port/web.md section 7 "What is missing" -->
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No sound.</strong></li>
    <li>
      <strong>A simple picture.</strong> It is a small renderer of its own (WebGPU, or WebGL2 where the browser has no
      WebGPU), not Assetto Corsa's: no shadows, no reflections, no sky.
    </li>
    <li><strong>One car on the track.</strong> Picking another car or track reloads the page.</li>
    <li>No wheel and no force feedback. Your own key bindings and saved setups are not read.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="need">What you need</h2>
  <!-- docs/web.md "Try it on this computer" and "How the page copes with a 441 MB file"; docs/port/web.md section 7 -->
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chrome or Edge on a computer.</strong> Other browsers were not tried.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your own Assetto Corsa folder</strong>, the one with <code>content</code> and <code>system</code> in it
      (<code>...\steamapps\common\assettocorsa</code>). The site holds no Assetto Corsa file.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Enough memory for the track.</strong> A big track needs about 1 to 1.5 GB in the tab while it loads. A
      computer with 4 GB may not manage Spa or Laguna Seca; a smaller track will do there.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    In the preview: open your folder, pick a car and a track, press <strong>Drive</strong>. The same cars and tracks
    load as on the desktop (<a href="/compatibility">the list</a>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Your files stay with you</h2>
  <!-- docs/web.md intro and its last paragraph; docs/port/web.md section 4.4 (the folder handle in IndexedDB); the preview's own app.js -->
  <ul>
    <li>
      You pick your Assetto Corsa folder in the browser's own folder dialog. The page then reads the files it needs
      straight from your disk, on your computer. <strong>Nothing is uploaded</strong> and nothing in the folder is
      changed.
    </li>
    <li>
      rustyac.com serves the preview's own files (a page, a script and the WebAssembly program) and nothing else. It
      never receives your game's files.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your browser remembers <em>which folder</em> you picked, in its own storage for this site, so the next visit
      needs one click at most. Chrome and Edge ask for permission once more on the next visit, unless you allowed the
      site on every visit. The game's files themselves are not copied anywhere.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="controls">Controls</h2>
  <!-- docs/web.md "Keys and pad" -->
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>Keyboard</th><th>Xbox pad</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          CONTROLS.map(([what, keys, pad]) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{what}</td>
              <td class="mono">{keys}</td>
              <td class="mono">{pad}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Left Shift is also the clutch, so use Right Shift for Shift+T and Shift+Y while moving. <kbd>]</kbd> and
    <kbd>[</kbd> are the two keys right of P. Keys pressed with Ctrl or Alt are left to the browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    Something broke? Tell us in the <a href={LINKS.discord} rel="noopener">Discord</a>. The full build is the
    <a href="/download">Windows download</a>.
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .launch {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .launch__desktop {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .launch__btn {
    min-height: 52px;
    padding: 0 24px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .launch__meta {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .launch__title {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .launch__phone {
    display: none;
  }

  /* the same rule the homepage uses to skip its 3D scene on phones (F2004Scene.astro) */
  @media (pointer: coarse) and (max-width: 900px) {
    .launch__desktop {
      display: none;
    }

    .launch__phone {
      display: block;
    }
  }
</style>
